The corrector equations, polynomial energy integrals, material model and
physical acceptance tolerances are unchanged. Additional Fourier coefficients are computed when the
original mode set has a larger envelope in reduced coordinates. Only the
original retained modes enter Q/G/Z and their inverses; no modes are added
to the consuming engine. The rectangle geometry and original cell-center
convention are preserved.

